The region between $y=9-x^{2}$ and $y=9-3x$, from $x=0$ to $x=3$, is rotated about the $x$-axis. Find the exact volume.
[tikz]\begin{tikzpicture}[x=12mm,y=5mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black},draw=black]
\fill[fill={rgb,255:red,212;green,232;blue,255}] (0,9) -- plot[domain=0:3,samples=60,variable=\x] ({\x},{9-(\x)*(\x)}) -- cycle;
\draw[->] (-0.4,0)--(4,0);
\draw[->] (0,-0.6)--(0,11);
\draw[thick] plot[domain=0:3,samples=60,variable=\x] ({\x},{9-(\x)*(\x)});
\draw[thick] (0,9)--(3,0);
\path (4,0) node[right] {$x$} (0,11) node[above] {$y$} (1.7,8.3) node[right] {$y=9-x^{2}$} (0.7,3.5) node[left] {$y=9-3x$};
\path (0,9) node[left] {$9$} (3,0) node[below] {$3$};
\end{tikzpicture}[/tikz]

The region enclosed by $y=3x$ and $y=x^{2}$ is rotated about the $x$-axis. Find the exact volume.
[tikz]\begin{tikzpicture}[x=12mm,y=5mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black},draw=black]
\fill[fill={rgb,255:red,212;green,232;blue,255}] (0,0)--(3,9)--plot[domain=3:0,samples=60,variable=\x] ({\x},{(\x)*(\x)})--cycle;
\draw[->] (-0.4,0)--(4,0);
\draw[->] (0,-0.6)--(0,11);
\draw[thick] (0,0)--(3.4,10.2);
\draw[thick] plot[domain=0:3.3,samples=60,variable=\x] ({\x},{(\x)*(\x)});
\path (4,0) node[right] {$x$} (0,11) node[above] {$y$} (1.3,5.4) node[left] {$y=3x$} (2.7,4.5) node[right] {$y=x^{2}$};
\end{tikzpicture}[/tikz]

The region between $y=9-x^{2}$ and $y=9-3x$ in the first quadrant is rotated about the $y$-axis. Find the exact volume.
[tikz]\begin{tikzpicture}[x=12mm,y=5mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black},draw=black]
\fill[fill={rgb,255:red,212;green,232;blue,255}] (0,9)--plot[domain=0:3,samples=60,variable=\x] ({\x},{9-(\x)*(\x)})--cycle;
\draw[->] (-0.4,0)--(4,0);
\draw[->] (0,-0.6)--(0,11);
\draw[thick] plot[domain=0:3,samples=60,variable=\x] ({\x},{9-(\x)*(\x)});
\draw[thick] (0,9)--(3,0);
\path (4,0) node[right] {$x$} (0,11) node[above] {$y$} (1.7,8.3) node[right] {$y=9-x^{2}$} (0.7,3.5) node[left] {$y=9-3x$};
\end{tikzpicture}[/tikz]

A region lies below $y=\sqrt{x-2}$ from $x=2$ to $x=8$. Its lower boundary is the $x$-axis for $2\le x\le5$ and $y=\sqrt{x-5}$ for $5\le x\le8$. Find its exact volume when rotated about the $x$-axis.
[tikz]\begin{tikzpicture}[x=8mm,y=14mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black},draw=black]
\fill[fill={rgb,255:red,212;green,232;blue,255}] (2,0)--plot[domain=2:8,samples=80,variable=\x] ({\x},{sqrt(\x-2)})--plot[domain=8:5,samples=60,variable=\x] ({\x},{sqrt(\x-5)})--cycle;
\draw[->] (0,0)--(9,0);
\draw[->] (0,-0.4)--(0,3.3);
\draw[thick] plot[domain=2:8,samples=80,variable=\x] ({\x},{sqrt(\x-2)});
\draw[thick] plot[domain=5:8,samples=60,variable=\x] ({\x},{sqrt(\x-5)});
\draw (8,{sqrt(3)})--(8,{sqrt(6)});
\path (9,0) node[right] {$x$} (0,3.3) node[above] {$y$} (4.5,2.6) node {$y=\sqrt{x-2}$} (7,0.8) node[right] {$y=\sqrt{x-5}$};
\foreach \v in {2,5,8}{\draw (\v,0)--(\v,-0.08);\path (\v,-0.08) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\v$};}
\end{tikzpicture}[/tikz]
